@startuml
!include style.puml

title PWasm Persistence Backend Capabilities
caption Wizard Engine commit 8b262f4c24497bd2c5abe37c4b84c40dd4a97bf8, 2026-07-02.
caption Durability semantics per BackendRegion implementation.

legend top
Backend capability matrix
|=  |= VolatileRegion |= PmemMmapRegion |= FileMmapRegion |
|<b>backend name()</b> | "volatile" | "pmem" | "file" |
|<b>isPersistent()</b> | false | true | true |
|<b>checkpointCost()</b> | FREE | CHEAP | EXPENSIVE |
|<b>backing</b> | Array<byte> (GC) | mmap MAP_SYNC (PMEM/DAX) | mmap file (block device) |
|<b>fresh=true</b> | new Array is zero-init | O_TRUNC + zero-fill | O_TRUNC + zero-fill |
|<b>prepareChangedRange</b> | no-op (true) | flushRange (CLWB*), set pending | mark hasDirtyChanges |
|<b>persistChanges</b> | no-op (true) | storeFence (SFENCE*) if pending | fdatasync(fd) if dirty |
|<b>persistRange</b> | no-op (true) | flushRange + storeFence | pageAlignedSyncRange (msync) |
endlegend

note bottom
* PMEM flushRange/storeFence (CLWB/SFENCE) are currently
no-op stubs (MmapRegionUtils) pending Virgil inline-asm;
PMEM durability is not yet functional. See ROADMAP Next Steps #2.

checkpointCost() drives the WAL's per-backend checkpoint
thresholds: FREE checkpoints on nearly every commit,
EXPENSIVE checkpoints lazily. Unknown backends default to
EXPENSIVE.

prepareChangedRange/persistChanges is the two-phase data
path (used by applyUpdate + maybeCheckpoint); persistRange
is the synchronous ordered path (used for WAL records and
superblock writes).
end note

@enduml
